WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.067 --> 00:00:12.789
One day a poor man came to visit an effendi while he was having tea.

2
00:00:12.790 --> 00:00:18.884
Effendi is a title of respect for a well-educated or wealthy man in the Middle East.

3
00:00:18.885 --> 00:00:24.201
The poor man said, "Effendi Nasreddin, I need your help.

4
00:00:24.202 --> 00:00:31.766
I don't know if you will help me. I am a poor man, a man with no money."

5
00:00:31.767 --> 00:00:37.617
The effendi looked at the man kindly. "I will help you," he said.

6
00:00:37.618 --> 00:00:39.554
"Tell me, what is wrong?"

7
00:00:39.555 --> 00:00:45.082
The poor man looked tired and hungry, and it took him a while to begin.

8
00:00:45.083 --> 00:00:48.840
"I have a problem ..." He paused suddenly.

9
00:00:48.841 --> 00:00:55.611
"Yes," said the effendi gently, "go on."

10
00:00:55.612 --> 00:01:01.945
"Yesterday I stopped in front of the door of a restaurant," the poor man said.

11
00:01:01.946 --> 00:01:06.201
"The restaurant belonged to a rich man. I ate nothing.

12
00:01:06.202 --> 00:01:11.676
I only smelled the food. However, the owner came out and noticed me.

13
00:01:11.677 --> 00:01:21.340
He said I was enjoying his food, and . . . and . . . he wanted me to pay him for the food."

14
00:01:21.341 --> 00:01:25.947
The poor man stopped. He turned his head and coughed.

15
00:01:25.948 --> 00:01:32.465
The effendi wondered if the man was crying, but he waited patiently for the man to continue.

16
00:01:32.466 --> 00:01:38.524
"Please, finish your story when you are ready," said the effendi.

17
00:01:38.525 --> 00:01:41.876
"Well," continued the poor man.

18
00:01:41.877 --> 00:01:46.874
"I, of course, had no money with me, so I couldn't pay him.

19
00:01:46.875 --> 00:01:52.433
He became very angry. He shouted and shouted until the judge came.

20
00:01:52.434 --> 00:01:55.436
The judge said I must appear in court today.

21
00:01:55.437 --> 00:01:58.395
He will tell me how I am to be punished.

22
00:01:58.396 --> 00:02:03.544
Please, effendi," begged the poor man, "can you help me?

23
00:02:03.545 --> 00:02:08.207
Can you say something to the judge?"

24
00:02:08.208 --> 00:02:14.126
The effendi offered the man some tea, and he sat thinking quietly while the man drank.

25
00:02:14.127 --> 00:02:17.841
When the man had finished his tea, the effendi spoke:

26
00:02:17.842 --> 00:02:25.596
"Yes, I will go to court with you. Let's go." And they left together.

27
00:02:25.597 --> 00:02:31.560
When the effendi and the poor man got to court, the rich man was already there.

28
00:02:31.561 --> 00:02:33.535
He was waiting for them.

29
00:02:33.536 --> 00:02:42.840
As soon as the rich man saw the poor man, he began shouting angrily, "This man owes me the price of one dinner!

30
00:02:42.841 --> 00:02:47.385
I want my money! These beggars are all alike!

31
00:02:47.386 --> 00:02:51.104
They live off the work of others!"

32
00:02:51.105 --> 00:02:54.961
It took the judge several minutes to calm the rich man down.

33
00:02:54.962 --> 00:02:59.017
"You see how angry he is?" said the judge.

34
00:02:59.018 --> 00:03:03.098
"You have filled yourself up on the smell of his restaurant.

35
00:03:03.099 --> 00:03:08.917
Yet you have not even paid him. You must pay him right now."

36
00:03:08.918 --> 00:03:13.635
After the effendi heard what the judge said, he stepped forward.

37
00:03:13.636 --> 00:03:19.448
He looked at the rich man and said, "Oh, sir, do not be so upset.

38
00:03:19.449 --> 00:03:22.847
This poor man is my brother, my elder brother.

39
00:03:22.848 --> 00:03:29.205
He is a poor man and he cannot pay you, so I will pay you instead."

40
00:03:29.206 --> 00:03:33.595
After he heard this, the rich man smiled a greedy smile.

41
00:03:33.596 --> 00:03:36.947
The effendi took a bag of coins from his belt.

42
00:03:36.948 --> 00:03:41.114
He bent down next to the rich man and shook the bag of coins.

43
00:03:41.115 --> 00:03:44.400
The coins jingled loudly.

44
00:03:44.401 --> 00:03:48.652
"Listen," said the effendi. "Do you hear that sound?"

45
00:03:48.653 --> 00:03:53.186
"Of course I hear!" said the rich man impatiently.

46
00:03:53.187 --> 00:03:57.624
"Well, then," answered the effendi, "the problem is solved.

47
00:03:57.625 --> 00:03:59.351
The debt is paid.

48
00:03:59.352 --> 00:04:03.581
My brother has smelled your food, and you have heard his money."

49
00:04:03.582 --> 00:04:08.570
The judge nodded. He was satisfied with the exchange.

50
00:04:08.571 --> 00:04:15.775
If the poor man only smelled the rich man's food, the rich man could only charge him the sound of his money.

51
00:04:15.776 --> 00:04:22.117
Afterward, the effendi took the arm of the poor man and handed him the bag of gold coins.

52
00:04:22.118 --> 00:04:28.376
"Go, my brother," said the effendi, "and taste the food you have smelled so much of."

53
00:04:28.377 --> 00:04:33.495
The poor man bowed respectfully and left.
